# Line endings, decided once (H8/S94, 2026-08-19).
#
# 896 tracked files were committed with CRLF, spread across Go, TypeScript,
# Python, Zig, Julia, Rust, Quint, the docs and more. Nothing enforced it and
# nothing depended on it — it was an accident of whichever editor wrote each
# file first. The cost was real and recurring: `mix format --check-formatted`
# went red on CI and passed locally on the same bytes; `gofmt -l ./go` printed
# 79 filenames; `cargo fmt` inside rust/ rewrote 140 files as a side effect of
# an unrelated change; and every agent or tool that read a file as text and
# wrote it back turned a four-line edit into a whole-file diff.
#
# The previous version of this file scoped the rule to Elixir alone and said
# widening it was "a separate decision, not a side effect of greening a gate".
# This is that decision, taken deliberately and on its own.
#
# Everything is normalised to LF in the repository. Git still checks out
# whatever the platform wants; only the stored bytes are fixed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells need CRLF at runtime, not as an accident.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.wasm binary
*.so   binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll  binary
*.a    binary
*.node binary
*.iso  binary
*.bin  binary
